Allow QEMU 11 to remove its keyboard and mouse interfaces before disconnecting
SPICE clients. SPICE 0.16.0 rejected those removals, leaving InputsChannel pointing
at QEMU's freed interfaces during server destruction. Release held keys, detach
the interfaces, and free server-owned state before the caller can free them.
The connected-client regression covers removal, replacement and destruction.

